# RE-CUT 2026-08-09, OWNER-AUTHORIZED.  These are correction-class values.
# `src/gw/ppm_accumulators.py` was closing the one-sided tau grid with an
# ELEMENTWISE Im -- `contrib = coeff_re * sigma_im + coeff_im * sigma_re`
# under a comment reading "Crossing window - keep Im[coeff*sigma]" -- where
# the sine sum needs the pair adjoint (Z - Z^dagger)/2i.  THE TWO COINCIDE
# ONLY AT k = -k, so the non-TRIM k of this deck carried a wrong Sigma_c.
# The fix landed on main at dd727216 (fix commit c80601b8) and turned this
# gate red BY CORRECTING IT; the numbers below are the corrected ones.  See
# the "Sigma_c breaks the k-star relation at the five non-TRIM k" row of
# tests/KNOWN_FAILURES.md for the full adjudication.
#
#   cut at       main @ dd727216 (2026-08-09), Perlmutter JID 56549382, -G=1
#                on 4x A100 under Shifter, LX_BASE_MODULE=lorrax_J070,
#                JAX_ENABLE_X64=1, restage_candidate_2026-08-08 .so pair
#                (device + host).  Preserved by pytest --basetemp at
#                /pscratch/sd/j/jackm/sigma_kstar_0809/_pytest_recut2/.
#   frozen at    1e64d83a on chore/gnppm-freeze-2026-08-09, 2026-08-09,
#                based on main @ 5b135f8e
#   re-verified  main @ 5b135f8e, Perlmutter JID 56555953, -G=1, same module
#                and .so pins: the gate's own comparison reports max|delta| =
#                0.000e+00, with 0 of 1620 compared cells differing AT ALL,
#                so what was cut at dd727216 is exactly what main produces
#                today.  The 9a730da8 dipole re-cut cannot reach this deck at
#                all -- bispinor_test.in takes the explicit head bypass
#                (vhead = whead_0freq = whead_imfreq = 0) and the fixture
#                ships no dipole.h5.
#   movement     sigC max|delta| = 7.7240e-03 eV against the 2026-08-01
#                values this replaces, 268 of 270 rows moved; sigX and VH
#                BIT-IDENTICAL (max|delta| = 0.000e+00), which is the control
#                placing the movement in Sigma_c and not in the static path.
#   Gamma        moves by 8.530e-04 eV rather than by zero, and that is the
#                deck behaving correctly: MoS2 has no inversion, TRS carries
#                the spinor rotation, and sigma^tau at Gamma is only
#                approximately complex-symmetric, so Gamma inherits a
#                correction of its own.  A TRIM k is exempt from this
#                correction only where k = -k makes the elementwise Im and
#                the pair adjoint the same operation.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT SEE, said here so it is not re-litigated: this is a
# sigma_diag file -- diagonal Sigma per band -- and a diagonal-Sigma
# observable cannot distinguish the window-level adjoint frozen here from
# the per-shard placement that is wrong by 5.2 eV over the off-diagonal
# cube; that off-diagonal defect class is covered by the sharded Hermiticity
# pair in tests/test_ppm_crossing_completion.py, NOT by this reference.
